  "response": "## What the finding actually points at\n\n`crime_00068` (`duplicate_component_shape`, medium / confidence 0.70) hashes a 9-line `<div>` subtree that appears verbatim in four files. Resolving the line ranges, it's the **form action bar** at the bottom of each invoice form — not the form body:\n\n| File | Lines |\n|---|---|\n| `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx` | 142–150 |\n| `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx` | 152–160 |\n| `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx` | 101–109 |\n| `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx` | 112–120 |\n\n```tsx\n<div className=\"mt-6 flex justify-end gap-4\">\n  <Link\n    href=\"/dashboard/invoices\"\n    className=\"flex h-10 items-center rounded-lg bg-gray-100 px-4 text-sm font-medium text-gray-600 transition-colors hover:bg-gray-200\"\n  >\n    Cancel\n  </Link>\n  <Button type=\"submit\">Create Invoice</Button>\n</div>\n```\n\n`grep` confirms exactly those four occurrences of `justify-end gap-4` in `dashboard/` — the finding is complete, not a sample.\n\n**The only thing that varies across all four is the submit label** (`Create Invoice` / `Edit Invoice`). The wrapper classes, the cancel `href`, the cancel label, and the 105-character cancel class string are byte-identical in every copy. That class string is the drift surface: it's a hand-rolled ghost-button that duplicates `Button`'s geometry (`flex h-10 items-center rounded-lg px-4 text-sm font-medium transition-colors`) with different colors, so a change to button height or radius has to land in five places and the `Link` copy will silently miss it.\n\n## One scope caveat before the design\n\n`final-example` and `starter-example` are **two independent Next.js apps**, each with its own `tsconfig.json` mapping `@/*` → `./*` (rooted at its own directory). No import can cross that boundary today, and this fixture is a tutorial starter/final pair — collapsing them would defeat the point of the starter (that's also why the scan shows ~30 other `final ↔ starter` duplicate findings, e.g. `crime_00048`, `crime_00058`, `crime_00059`).\n\nSo the consolidation is **one shared component per app, 2 call sites each** — not one component for all four. A single cross-app component would require promoting `app/ui/` into a workspace package, which is a much larger change and the wrong call for a tutorial repo. I've designed for the per-app version below; the API is identical in both, so it lifts into a shared package unchanged if that ever becomes desirable.\n\n## Proposed component\n\n**New file (×2):** `app/ui/invoices/form-actions.tsx` in each app.\n\n```tsx\nimport Link from 'next/link';\nimport { Button } from '@/app/ui/button';\n\nexport function FormActions({\n  cancelHref,\n  submitLabel,\n  cancelLabel = 'Cancel',\n  children,\n}: {\n  /** Where Cancel navigates. Required — no invoice-shaped default. */\n  cancelHref: string;\n  /** Submit button content. ReactNode so callers can pass an icon. */\n  submitLabel: React.ReactNode;\n  cancelLabel?: React.ReactNode;\n  /** Leading slot: extra actions rendered left of Cancel (e.g. Delete). */\n  children?: React.ReactNode;\n}) {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"mt-6 flex justify-end gap-4\">\n      {children}\n      <Link\n        href={cancelHref}\n        className=\"flex h-10 items-center rounded-lg bg-gray-100 px-4 text-sm font-medium text-gray-600 transition-colors hover:bg-gray-200\"\n      >\n        {cancelLabel}\n      </Link>\n      <Button type=\"submit\">{submitLabel}</Button>\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\n### Public API\n\n**Props**\n\n| Prop | Type | Required | Justification |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `cancelHref` | `string` | yes | Identical in all four call sites *today*, but it's a route — defaulting it to `/dashboard/invoices` would bake an invoice assumption into a generic UI component and make the next caller's bug silent. Required and explicit. |\n| `submitLabel` | `React.ReactNode` | yes | The one genuine variation. `ReactNode`, not `string`, so `login-form`'s `Log in <ArrowRightIcon />` shape can adopt this later without an API break. |\n| `cancelLabel` | `React.ReactNode` | no, `'Cancel'` | Speculative — add only if a second caller needs it. Listed because it costs nothing and is the obvious next ask. |\n\n**Slots**\n\n| Slot | Contract |\n|---|---|\n| `children` | Leading action slot, rendered **before** Cancel so the submit button stays rightmost under `justify-end`. Intended for destructive/secondary actions (a `Delete invoice` button on the edit form). Empty in both current call sites. |\n\nDeliberately **not** in the API: `className` (a style escape hatch reopens exactly the drift this closes), a `submit` override slot (if you're replacing the button, don't use this component), and pending/disabled state (`Button` already forwards `ButtonHTMLAttributes`; put it there, not here).\n\n**Rendering constraint:** no `'use client'` directive. `Link` and `Button` are both server-safe (`button.tsx` is a plain `clsx` wrapper), and `starter-example/create-form.tsx` is currently a Server Component while `edit-form.tsx` is a Client Component. Leaving `FormActions` server-compatible keeps it usable from both; adding `'use client'` would silently pull the starter's create form into the client bundle.\n\n## Files that change\n\n**Added (2)**\n- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/form-actions.tsx`\n- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/form-actions.tsx`\n\n**Edited (4)** — each loses 9 lines of JSX, drops its now-unused `Link` and `Button` imports, and gains one `FormActions` import:\n\n| File | Replaces | With |\n|---|---|---|\n| `final-example/…/create-form.tsx` | 142–150 | `<FormActions cancelHref=\"/dashboard/invoices\" submitLabel=\"Create Invoice\" />` |\n| `final-example/…/edit-form.tsx` | 152–160 | `<FormActions cancelHref=\"/dashboard/invoices\" submitLabel=\"Edit Invoice\" />` |\n| `starter-example/…/create-form.tsx` | 101–109 | `<FormActions cancelHref=\"/dashboard/invoices\" submitLabel=\"Create Invoice\" />` |\n| `starter-example/…/edit-form.tsx` | 112–120 | `<FormActions cancelHref=\"/dashboard/invoices\" submitLabel=\"Edit Invoice\" />` |\n\nNet ≈ −36 lines of JSX, +2 files. No behaviour change: same DOM, same classes, same route. `Link` stays imported only where else used — in all four files it's used solely by this footer, so the import goes.\n\n**Verification:** rendered markup is byte-identical, so a DOM snapshot before/after is the check. Re-running `crimes scan --format json` should drop `crime_00068` entirely (the shape now has one definition per app, below the ≥2-file threshold).\n\n## What this doesn't fix\n\nTwo adjacent duplications sit in the same files and are worth more than the footer, but neither is what `crime_00068` flagged — flagging them rather than folding them in:\n\n1. **The status radio group** (`final` create 92–125 / edit 100–135, `starter` create 65–98 / edit 74–109) is duplicated four times and is where the `\"pending\"` / `\"paid\"` literals live that `crime_00018` and `crime_00019` charge as *Duplicated Role / Status / Plan Check* (agent_risk 0.36 — higher than the footer's 0.28). An `<InvoiceStatusRadios defaultStatus?: InvoiceStatus>` would retire the shape duplication and both policy findings at once. It's also where real drift has *already happened*: `final/create-form.tsx:100` has `text-white-600` (not a Tailwind class — the pending radio's text color is dead) where the other three have `text-gray-600`, and `final/edit-form.tsx:109,125` dropped `cursor-pointer` that the other copies keep. That's this exact failure mode caught in the act.\n\n2. **The error blocks** in `final-example` — `{state.errors?.X && …map(error => <p className=\"mt-2 text-sm text-red-500\">)}` appears three times per file, six across the two forms, and `edit-form.tsx:148` uses `my-2` where `create-form.tsx:138` uses `mt-2`. A `<FieldError id errors={state.errors?.customerId} />` collapses all six. Note this one exists only in `final-example`; the starter forms have no error rendering yet, which is the tutorial's whole point — so it's a per-app fix, not a four-file one.\n\nBoth are larger extractions than the footer and I'd land them as separate changes.",
